{"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Explanation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SecurityPosture"],"anchor":"Explanation","generated":true}],"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Swidux’s plugin system is a single protocol (","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","isActive":true},{"text":") with four lifecycle hooks and an ordered registry (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"). All store extensibility flows through this contract. The built-in ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true},{"text":" use it, and so do domain-specific features like killswitch enforcement and paywall management.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"The-Dispatch-Lifecycle","text":"The Dispatch Lifecycle","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every call to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.send()"},{"text":" drives plugins through a four-phase lifecycle:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing","code":["plugins.willReduce(state:action:)      \/\/ 1. Pre-reduce (read-only state)","appReducer.reduce(state:action:...)    \/\/ 2. App reducer runs","pluginEffects = plugins.reduce(...)    \/\/ 3. Plugin reducers run","plugins.afterReduce(state:action:)     \/\/ 4. Post-reduce cleanup"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The generic ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","isActive":true},{"text":" implements this lifecycle internally. You don’t write ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"send()"},{"text":" by hand — ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store.send()"},{"text":" handles packing, reducing, plugin hooks, unpacking, and effect dispatch.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A fifth method, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush()"},{"text":", runs once at shutdown to drain async buffers.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"All four hooks have default no-op implementations. Each plugin overrides only what it needs.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Core-Plugins-vs-Domain-Plugins","text":"Core Plugins vs Domain Plugins","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The plugin system serves two structurally different roles. Recognizing which one a plugin fills determines where it lives, which hooks it uses, and how it couples to the host app.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"anchor":"Core-Plugins","text":"Core Plugins","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"text":" are ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"action-agnostic infrastructure","type":"text"}]},{"text":". They never inspect the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Action"},{"text":" type, never dispatch actions, and never return effects. They couple only to the shape of state:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" needs keypaths to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" properties.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" needs ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State: Equatable"},{"text":" so it can snapshot and compare.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Because they don’t touch actions, they work with any app that uses Swidux — no wiring required beyond construction.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Domain-Plugins","text":"Domain Plugins","type":"heading","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Killswitch, parental gate, and paywall plugins are ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"domain-specific modules","type":"text"}]},{"text":" that ship as separate library targets (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxKillswitch"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxParentalGate"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPaywall"},{"text":"). They own their own state slices and action enums, dispatch effects, and must be explicitly wired into the host app’s root types.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each domain plugin stores three wiring pieces:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["private let stateKeyPath: WritableKeyPath<RootState, FeatureState>","private let toRootAction: @Sendable (FeatureAction) -> RootAction","private let extractAction: @Sendable (RootAction) -> FeatureAction?"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The host app provides these at init — the plugin never assumes a specific root type.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Importing-at-call-sites","text":"Importing at call sites","type":"heading","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Because each domain plugin ships as a ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"separate library target","type":"text"}]},{"text":", its state and action types are defined in that module — not in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Swidux"},{"text":". A common convention is to re-export core Swidux from ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppState.swift"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@_exported import Swidux"},{"text":", but that re-exports ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"core Swidux only","type":"text"}]},{"text":"; it does not re-export the plugin modules.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"So any file that reads a plugin-owned slice (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.analytics.*"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.paywall.*"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.killswitch.*"},{"text":", …) or dispatches a plugin action (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsAction"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallAction"},{"text":", …) must import that plugin’s module in ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"that","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" file:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"touches "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.analytics.*"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsAction"},{"type":"text","text":" → "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import SwiduxAnalytics"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"touches "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.paywall.*"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallAction"},{"type":"text","text":" → "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import SwiduxPaywall"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"touches only "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.ui"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".ui(...)"},{"text":" (app-module types) → nothing extra","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The easy case to forget is a ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"View","type":"text"}]},{"text":" that reads the slice for display — ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppState.swift"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppAction.swift"},{"type":"text","text":" already import the module, but the View is a different file. Without the import you get:"}]},{"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing","code":["property 'isOptedOut' is not available due to missing import of defining module 'SwiduxAnalytics'","property 'isPro' is not available due to missing import of defining module 'SwiduxPaywall'"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is to add "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Swidux<Plugin>"},{"type":"text","text":" to that file."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Comparison","anchor":"Comparison"},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Core Plugins","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Domain Plugins","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Action knowledge","type":"text"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"None","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Full — extracts and lifts actions","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Lifecycle hooks","type":"text"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"text":", plus ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"text":" to react to every dispatch","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Returns effects","type":"text"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"No","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Yes","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"State coupling","type":"text"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Keypath to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"text":" constraint","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Keypath to plugin’s own state slice","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Wiring","type":"text"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Construction only","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Keypath + action lifter + action extractor","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Target","type":"text"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Core ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Swidux"},{"text":" library","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Separate library target","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Opt-in","type":"text"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Instantiate and register","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Add state, action case, and register","type":"text"}]}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"The Decision Rule","anchor":"The-Decision-Rule"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Does the plugin need to know your action type? If ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"no","type":"text"}]},{"text":", it’s a core plugin — put it in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Swidux"},{"text":" and use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"text":". If ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"yes","type":"text"}]},{"text":", it’s a domain plugin — give it its own target and handle its own actions in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"text":". A domain plugin that must also react to every dispatch, as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsPlugin"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FeatureFlagsPlugin"},{"text":" do, adds ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}],"type":"aside","style":"important","name":"Important"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Hook Selection Guide","anchor":"Hook-Selection-Guide"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"willReduce(state:action:)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — Capture state ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"before"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" the reducer mutates it. State is read-only. Use for snapshots (undo) or pre-mutation analytics.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce(state:action:) -> Effect?"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — Handle domain-specific actions ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"after"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" the app reducer. Mutate the plugin’s state slice and return effects. This is the only hook that can dispatch actions or do async work.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce(state:action:)"}]},{"text":" — Observe state ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"after"}]},{"text":" all reducing is done. Use for persistence draining, logging, or metrics. Cannot return effects.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush() async"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — Shutdown hook. Flush pending async buffers (persistence writes, analytics batches). Called once when the app exits.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Registration Order","anchor":"Registration-Order"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" executes plugins in registration order. Recommended ordering:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let plugins = PluginHost<AppState, AppAction>()","plugins.register(undoPlugin)         \/\/ 1. Must snapshot before any mutation","plugins.register(persistencePlugin)  \/\/ 2. Drains changelogs after reducer","plugins.register(killswitchPlugin)   \/\/ 3. Domain plugins in any order","plugins.register(paywallPlugin)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Undo must come first — it snapshots state in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"text":", before the app reducer or any plugin modifies it. Persistence typically comes next so its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"text":" drain sees the final state. Domain plugins handle their own actions in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"text":", so their relative order rarely matters.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Service-Result Actions and Transition Observation","anchor":"Service-Result-Actions-and-Transition-Observation","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"service-result action","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" — ","type":"text"},{"code":"PaywallPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"customerInfoUpdated","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KillswitchPlugin"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"verdictReceived"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FeatureFlagsPlugin"},{"text":"’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshSucceeded"},{"text":" — fires on ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"every","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" fetch, refresh, or stream tick, not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only when the value changed, and unconditionally writes its payload to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"state slice. The payload is frequently identical to what is already there","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(a re-delivered entitlement, an unchanged remote config).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Do ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"not","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" map analytics or side effects to the raw service-result action:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it fires duplicates by design. Observe the ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"state slice","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — or a value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"derived from it — instead.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"State observation is already deduplicated by the framework. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store.send"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"packs the observer into a value-type snapshot, lets reducers mutate the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"snapshot, then writes back via ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State.apply"},{"text":". For a leaf slice that write","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is a plain assignment whose ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"text":" setter equality-gates ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"values, so a slice whose value did not change emits no notification — and a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"value-diffing consumer such as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsIdentity.userProperties"},{"text":" (which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsPlugin"},{"text":" re-evaluates and diffs every non-analytics dispatch) sees exactly the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"real transitions. This dedup is a property of the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store"},{"text":", not of any","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"per-plugin guard, so a no-op service-result cycle is silent to state","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"observers without any extra reducer logic.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Next Steps","anchor":"Next-Steps"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin"},{"text":" — Step-by-step guide to creating a domain plugin","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide"},{"text":" — Configure the built-in persistence plugin","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo"},{"tex